# Valunxt — environment.
# Copy to .env.local and fill in what applies. In development every value has a
# working default (a local XAMPP MySQL: root, no password), so a fresh clone
# runs with none of this set. A production build needs the database and admin
# session settings below: without DB_HOST it cannot reach its data, and without
# a session key the admin panel refuses to sign anyone in.
#
# All of these stay on the server except NEXT_PUBLIC_* values, which Next.js
# inlines into browser code. Never put a password or key in a NEXT_PUBLIC_ name.

# ---- Public site ----------------------------------------------------------
# The origin used for canonical URLs, Open Graph tags and sitemap entries when
# the request host is not authoritative (a build, a preview deployment). The
# main domain is valunxt.com, which is also the default when this is unset.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_ORIGIN=https://valunxt.com

# ---- Database -------------------------------------------------------------
# The imported www.valunxt.com database (README, "Database"): blog posts, leads,
# page SEO, redirects, the client portal and everything else the admin panel
# manages. Required in production. Unset in development, the site uses
# 127.0.0.1:3306, user root, no password, database valunxt_capital_admin.
# scripts/import-valunxt-db.mjs reads these from this file too.
# DB_HOST=127.0.0.1
# DB_PORT=3306
# DB_NAME=valunxt_capital_admin
# DB_USER=
# DB_PASS=

# ---- Admin panel ----------------------------------------------------------
# Signs the admin session cookie and the panel's CSRF tokens. Set a long random
# value (e.g. `openssl rand -base64 48`) before the panel is reachable from the
# internet. Without it the key is derived from DB_PASS; with neither, a
# production build refuses to sign anyone in.
# ADMIN_SESSION_SECRET=

# The administrator seeded into an empty `vx_users` table on first connection.
# An imported database already has its accounts, so this only applies to a
# fresh, empty install. The sign-in screen prints these in development only; on
# a deployed panel an account still using the default password is sent to
# change it.
# ADMIN_DEFAULT_NAME=Valunxt Admin
# ADMIN_DEFAULT_EMAIL=admin@valunxtcapital.com
# ADMIN_DEFAULT_PASS=Admin@123
